      intro: `A teething baby is hard to watch, and every shop has a shelf of products that promise relief. Several of them are either unproven or unsafe. The US Food and Drug Administration (FDA) says benzocaine and lidocaine products should not be used for teething pain, and it has received reports of deaths and serious injuries linked to teething jewellery such as amber necklaces. The NHS does not recommend homeopathic teething products, and says not to give honey until a child is over 1 year old. What the official bodies do recommend is much simpler: gum massage, something firm and cool to chew, comfort. This guide goes through the common remedies one by one, says what each body actually says, and notes where local advice differs. It is general information, not medical advice for your baby.`,
